  "description": "Late spring. The streets of Hongseong were soaked and bustling under the weight of the season. Exhausted and emotionally drained under her parents’ contempt and coldness, Seo-Hee crosses paths by chance with a notorious playboy known for his promiscuity.\n\n *\"Ah... I didn’t mean to take it this far.\"\n\"Guess I’ll be staying the night.\"* \n\nA man who freely drifts between tenderness and rudeness. A man who treats people like fleeting amusements. A man who scoffs at the idea of a beautiful fairytale, calling it a hollow illusion , Joo Tae-Baek. Wrapped in brilliance and danger, he crashes into Seo-Hee like a violent wave, shaking her to her core.\n\n *\"Okay. I’ll keep your secret.\"\n\"...You mean it?\"\n\"Sure, if you let me rock your world once, nice and loud.\"*\n\nA dirty fling. A fleeting rush. \"No need to overthink it.\" She thought if she let herself be consumed by him, even a false love might be better than nothing. And so, she willingly threw herself into the fire, a lighthearted affair that was anything but; Was she out of her mind? Who the hell taught her that this was how you seduce a man?\n\n *\"So... we’re done now, right?\"*\n\nSeo-Hee tilted her head slightly toward the completely dazed Tae-Baek. \n\n*\"I need to be gone before midnight.\"* \n\nSo then... Who really got burned in the end?\n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)",
